        "original_id": "bd45e2e6-651c-5add-8b53-470945fda7b6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lee Tamahori, Robert Redford, Pete Dexter, Nick Nolte, Jennifer Connelly, Chazz Palminteri, Michael Madsen, Chris Penn, Melanie Griffith, Andrew McCarthy, Treat Williams, John Malkovich\n- Films: Once Were Warriors, Die Another Day, Mulholland Falls\n- Topics: filmmaking, acting, directing, producing, environmentalism, philanthropy\n\nFacts:\n- Lee Tamahori was born on 17 June 1950 and is a New Zealand filmmaker.\n- Robert Redford, born Charles Robert Redford Jr. on August 18, 1936, is an American actor, director, producer, businessman, environmentalist, and philanthropist.\n- Lee Tamahori is best known for directing the 1994 film Once Were Warriors.\n- Mulholland Falls is a 1996 American neo-noir crime thriller film directed by Lee Tamahori and written by Pete Dexter.\n- Mulholland Falls stars Nick Nolte, Jennifer Connelly, Chazz Palminteri, Michael Madsen, Chris Penn, Melanie Griffith, Andrew McCarthy, Treat Williams, and John Malkovich.\n- Lee Tamahori is also known for directing the 2002 James Bond film Die Another Day.",
